  "/goal You are opening LANE L3 of the observability mission. Your worktree already exists at .worktrees/obs-lane-3 on branch obs-lane-3-runner-cause, based on 7a3ff39 which contains BOTH the merged L1 store foundation and the fully-approved L2 capture package — read them, never modify them, they belong to other lanes. YOUR TWO TICKETS, in this order: S06 t_5504afe0 the runner binding, then S07 t_9f4e5bfb the cause-chain retrofit. Read each with: hermes kanban --board observability-loop show <id> — always put --board observability-loop BEFORE the verb, never run boards switch. Each ticket body is your authoritative file contract, tests glob, RED to GREEN obligation and forbidden list. Post WORKER CLAIM per slice. WHAT THESE SLICES ARE. S06 binds capture into the runner: the task seam and the provider-gateway seam, so errors thrown in the product's main work loop are actually caught. S07 is the cause-chain retrofit, and it is the reason root-tracing is possible at all: the codebase's TypedDomainError takes no cause argument, so today every catch-and-rethrow severs the chain — 49 wraps across 492 throw sites. Without S07 no error can be traced past its first wrapper. FOUR THINGS CARRY IN. First, S06 OWNS A PROOF RELOCATED BY ARCHITECTURE: the workspace-root resolution of @debateai/obs-capture, asserted from the WORKSPACE ROOT and never by package self-reference, which is disallowed as evidence because it needs no link and was exactly the false positive that made an earlier slice's green meaningless; include a @debateai/db control proving method and environment, and confirm the deep-import refusal survives real linkage. Second, THE ZONE BOUNDARY IS NOW SEMANTIC, not a line range: it is the single top-level if options.registration block in buildApi containing exactly the three named auth mounts in order, located at check time by resolveZoneRouteMountRegion in tests/support/zone-boundary.ts, which already exists in your base. NEVER write inside that region, and never quote a line number as the definition — the old range rotted eleven times in six days. Third, V RULED: no filesystem metadata on zone files at all, no reads, imports, listing, hash, size, mtime or mode, and no SQL against identity; and id parameters use DECLARED KINDS, not shapes. Fourth, the typecheck baseline is EMPTY at current dev but your lane base is older, so measure honestly and STATE WHICH BASE you measured from; the binding rule is ZERO diagnostics in your own touched paths. Standing lessons, nine review rounds deep: prove by calling the real thing, never by reading text back; never weaken an assertion to reach green; never strengthen a test by weakening the system; test the deployment path not just the fixture path; keep file colon line frames. End each slice at READY FOR PEER REVIEW posted as that ticket's comment with exact RED to GREEN output. No push, no merge, no Done. If two plan properties conflict, BLOCK and post it — you never choose between them. Then stop." \
